6. Let $a, b, c, d, m, n$ all be positive real numbers.
$P=\sqrt{a b}+\sqrt{c d}, Q=\sqrt{m a+n c} \cdot \sqrt{\frac{b}{m}+\frac{d}{n}}$, then,
(A) $P \geqslant Q$;
(B) $P \leqslant Q$;
(C) $P < Q$;
(D) The relationship between $P$ and $Q$ is uncertain and depends on the sizes of $m$ and $n$.

Three. (25 points) Given positive real numbers $x, y, z$ satisfying
$$
\begin{array}{l}
x y + y z + z x \neq 1, \\
\frac{\left(x^{2}-1\right)\left(y^{2}-1\right)}{x y} + \frac{\left(y^{2}-1\right)\left(z^{2}-1\right)}{y z} + \\
\frac{\left(z^{2}-1\right)\left(x^{2}-1\right)}{z x} = 4 .
\end{array}
$$
(1) Find the value of $\frac{1}{x y} + \frac{1}{y z} + \frac{1}{z x}$;
(2) Prove:
$$
\begin{array}{l}
9(x+y)(y+z)(z+x) \\
\geqslant 8 x y z(x y + y z + z x) .
\end{array}
$$

